//! The `margin-top` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the
//! [margin
//! area](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Box_model/Introduction#margin_area)
//! on the top of an element. A positive value places it farther from its neighbors, while a negative
//! value places it closer.
//!
//! Initial: 0. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: refer to the width of the containing block.
//!
//! Grammar: <length-percentage> | auto | <anchor-size()>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-box-4/#propdef-margin-top
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/margin-top
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

